This is an explanation of how some of these customized resources are set up.You may notice that there are some .view files that are not included in theCodeWarrior project for this example.  This is deliberate.  These .view filesare used to edit the customizations for the view layout for a specific locale.The French layout, for example, requires a little more space for one of thetext fields and a wider button.  It has also been layed out a little differentlyfrom the base (English) to allow for a taller but narrower image.Once the view is customized the resulting 'View' resource is copied, using a resource editor, and pasted into the associated .rsrc file and the ID is changedby adding the appropriate locale offset.Also please note that it is necessary in some cases to provide customizedTxSt resources.  You can find a good example in the Japanese.rsrc file.  Inthis particular case 'Osaka' has been substituted for 'Monaco' and one ofthe sized has been increased.